+
+## Historical computer names in retained anchors
+
+A renamed Windows installation may retain its oldest System record under its
+previous computer name. The default collector rejects that witness. A reviewed
+configuration may optionally include `historicalAnchorSha256`, a mapping from
+`System` or `Application` to the SHA-256 of the exact retained anchor XML encoded
+as UTF-8. Preserve the original native export and verify that this historical
+record belongs to the current local log before approving the configuration.
+The pin is an explicit operator attestation, not proof of machine continuity.
+The pinned record must precede both the current Windows boot and query start.
+Both before and after witnesses must match it exactly. All queried window events
+still require the current host name. Rotation, record replacement or a pin change
+requires a new reviewed configuration; no event log should be cleared to make
+this check pass. Pins enter the query identity and configuration digest.
+
+For a local WSL deployment, use the effective Windows execution policy without
+policy overrides. A `RemoteSigned` policy may treat `\\wsl.localhost` as a
+remote origin; review the local UNC zone classification. Also verify WSLInterop
+registration and the Windows PowerShell 5.1 module search path. Test actual helper
+execution, as dependency probes do not read event logs. Local deployment and
+model runs on an unqualified machine do not acquire departmental qualification.
